SLUG: locations/kanpur.html
TITLE: Packers & Movers in Kanpur — home & office shifting
DESC: Shifting within Kanpur and out of it, run from our own office on Swaroop Nagar. The localities we cover, what Kanpur buildings and lanes actually require, and how a move here is priced.
HEADING: Packers &amp; movers in Kanpur
LEAD: This is the city we are based in, not one we cover from somewhere else. The survey, the crew and the coordinator are all local.
CRUMBS: Home|/ ; Areas we cover|/locations.html ; Kanpur|
---

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split is-wide-left">
        <div>
          <h2>A Kanpur move, run by people who live here</h2>

          <!-- Written once, in js/config.js, so the city page and the card on
               /locations.html can never disagree about what we claim to cover. -->
          <p class="lead" data-area-intro="kanpur" hidden></p>

          <p>
            That matters more in Kanpur than it does in a newer city. The
            difference between a flat in Civil Lines and a house off Birhana
            Road is not the distance between them — it is whether a goods
            vehicle can get within fifty metres of the door, whether there is a
            lift, and what hour the building will let a crew start. Those three
            answers decide the vehicle, the crew size and the price, and they
            are the first things we establish at survey.
          </p>
          <p>
            We would rather tell you at the survey that your staircase turns a
            wardrobe into a two-person forty-minute job than discover it on the
            morning and ask you for more money.
          </p>

          <div class="btn-row mt-6">
            <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact.html" data-open-callback>Get a Kanpur quote</a>
            <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/services.html">All services</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-pin"/></svg></span>
          <h3>Localities we cover</h3>
          <p>
            Across the city, north and south of the Ganga canal. If your area
            is not on this list, ask — it almost certainly still works.
          </p>
          <!-- Filled from serviceAreas[].localities in js/config.js. -->
          <ul class="ticks" data-localities="kanpur" hidden></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-sunk">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Local knowledge</span>
        <h2>What a Kanpur move actually involves</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          None of this is about the driving. It is about the hundred metres at
          each end.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>The old city lanes</h3>
          <p>
            Around Birhana Road, Naya Ganj, Sisamau and the older Gumti lanes,
            a full-size truck often simply cannot turn in. The answer is a
            smaller vehicle doing two runs, or a shuttle from a larger vehicle
            parked on the main road. Either way it is a decision made at survey
            and written into the quote, not improvised on the day.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Society timing rules</h3>
          <p>
            Many of the newer apartment blocks in Swaroop Nagar, Vikas Nagar
            and along the Kalyanpur side restrict shifting to fixed hours and
            require a gate pass arranged in advance. A crew that cannot begin
            before ten and must stop by six has roughly seven usable hours,
            which changes what can honestly be promised for a single day.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Lifts, and the lack of them</h3>
          <p>
            A great deal of Kanpur's housing stock is three and four storeys
            with no lift, and plenty of the lifts that do exist will not take a
            mattress or a tall almirah standing up. We ask for the floor number
            and whether there is a lift at both ends, because the stair carry
            is the single biggest variable in the labour on a Kanpur job.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Traffic windows and road work</h3>
          <p>
            Crossing between the two halves of the city in the late afternoon
            is slow, and wherever metro or drainage work is active the approach
            roads narrow further. We plan loading for early in the day for this
            reason, which is also when the heat is survivable for a crew
            carrying furniture down stairs.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Industrial and commercial moves</h3>
          <p>
            Kanpur still has a great deal of small manufacturing and trade, and
            an office or workshop move here often means machinery, stock and
            paper records rather than desks alone. Those need weighing up
            individually — tell us what the heaviest single item is and whether
            it can leave through the door it came in by.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Monsoon and summer</h3>
          <p>
            Between July and September, cartons and mattresses need covering
            and loading has to happen in breaks in the rain, which makes the
            day less predictable. May and June are the opposite problem: we
            start at first light and the crew works shorter stretches. Neither
            stops a move; both change the schedule, so we say so in advance.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>Moving out of Kanpur</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            Intercity work goes on a dedicated vehicle by default, with a
            shared part-load as the cheaper option when you can accept a wider
            delivery window.
          </p>
          <p>
            These are the routes we are asked for most often. Road distances
            are approximate and given only to show the scale of the journey —
            the delivery window for your move is agreed in writing before the
            vehicle leaves, and we do not quote an arrival hour we cannot keep.
          </p>

          <div class="table-wrap mt-6">
            <table class="table">
              <caption class="sr-only">Common intercity routes from Kanpur with approximate road distances</caption>
              <thead>
                <tr><th scope="col">From Kanpur to</th><th scope="col">Approx. road distance</th></tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Lucknow</td><td>90 km</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Prayagraj</td><td>200 km</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Jhansi</td><td>220 km</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Agra</td><td>290 km</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Varanasi</td><td>330 km</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Delhi &amp; NCR</td><td>480 km</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Jaipur</td><td>630 km</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Kolkata</td><td>1,000 km</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Mumbai</td><td>1,350 km</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Bengaluru</td><td>1,800 km</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p class="text-sm mt-4">
            Not listed is not the same as not possible. Send both addresses and
            we will say plainly whether it is a job we can do well.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>Questions about moving in Kanpur</h2>
          <div class="faq mt-6" data-faq>
            <details>
              <summary>Do you cover the whole of Kanpur?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                Yes — the city and its immediate outskirts, on both sides of
                the canal. Our office is on Swaroop Nagar, so nothing in Kanpur is
                far enough away to need a different crew. The areas listed
                above are the ones we work in most; if yours is not named, ask
                rather than assuming.
              </p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Can a truck reach my lane?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                In much of the older city, not a full-size one. That is a
                normal situation here and it has a normal answer: a smaller
                vehicle, more than one run, or a shuttle from a larger vehicle
                on the main road. What we will not do is turn up with the wrong
                vehicle and treat the extra work as your problem.
              </p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>How much notice do you need?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                For a local move within Kanpur, often only a few days, because
                no long-distance vehicle has to be committed. Intercity moves
                are easier with a week or more, especially at month end when
                tenancies change over. Ask for your date — if a crew is free we
                will say so, and if not we will tell you instead of overbooking.
              </p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>How is a Kanpur move priced?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                Four things: the volume being moved, the distance, how much
                packing you want us to do, and the access at each address —
                floor, lift and how far the vehicle can park from the door. We
                survey first, in person or by video call, and the quote is
                issued in writing with those parts itemised. We do not publish
                a fixed rate card, because a moving price given without seeing
                the inventory is not a price anyone can be held to.
              </p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Can you move a car or a two-wheeler as well?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                Yes, in a covered carrier rather than driven, with the condition
                photographed at both ends. It is usually arranged alongside a
                household move out of Kanpur.
                <a href="/services/vehicle-transport.html">More on vehicle transport</a>.
              </p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Where exactly is your office?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                113/186, Swaroop Nagar, Kanpur 208002. You are welcome to come and talk it through in person
                before booking anything.
                <a href="/contact.html">Contact details and hours</a>.
              </p></div>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

